{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I sit here alone on the banks of the river
[D]The lonesome wind [G]blows the water rolls [D]high
[D]I hear a voice [G]calling out there in the [D]darkness
[D]I sit here [A]alone too lonesome to [D]cry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Oh the water rolls high on the river at midnight
[D]I sit on the shore to grieve and to cry
[D]The woman I love she left me this morning
[D]With no one to [A]love or kiss me [D]goodnight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
We met there one night by the banks of the river
Sat there holding hands and making our vows
Swore we'd never part and be happy forever
But a new love she's found she's gone to me now
{end_of_verse}
